.Dd October 18, 2026
.Dt TZFS.CONF 5
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm tzfs.conf
.Nd configuration file for the bsdfilesystem storage daemon
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Pa /Capabilities/Config/bsdfilesystem.ucl
configures
.Xr bsdfilesystem 8 .
It is a
.Xr libucl 3
document with optional keys and the defaults listed below.
Under BSD Integrity Protection (BIP), the file is required, must be owned by
root without group or other write permission, and must reside on the
read-only authenticated system filesystem.
The kernel's BIP protections prevent replacement of that filesystem and its
backing storage; a read-only flag alone does not authenticate policy.
Capsule's boot storage assignment selects and retains the policy file;
SwitchBoard and the provider parse duplicates of that same opened object.
The command-line override is rejected under BIP.
Outside BIP, only an absent default policy file permits built-in defaults.
A file explicitly selected with
.Fl c
must exist, belong to the daemon's effective user, and not be group or
other writable.
.Pp
Supplied policy must be a regular file no larger than 1 MiB.
Malformed input, unknown or duplicate keys, truncated values, embedded NULs,
control characters in strings, invalid types, and duplicate path grants are
fatal startup errors.
Includes and macros are rejected, and variable expansion is disabled.
An invalid policy is never replaced by built-in defaults.
The retired BIP
.Va access
key is rejected, including an empty array.
.Sh KEYS
.Bl -tag -width ".Va default_refquota"
.It Va pool
Name of the ZFS pool that backs
.Pa /Capabilities .
Setting it recomputes the root layout below unless those are overridden
explicitly.
Default
.Ql zroot .
.It Va roots.base
Base dataset for the capability storage tree.
Setting it recomputes omitted persistent and ephemeral roots.
Default
.Ql <pool>/Capabilities .
.It Va roots.persistent
Parent of persistent per-application datasets.
Default
.Ql <base>/Data .
.It Va roots.ephemeral
Parent of ephemeral datasets, created on service start and destroyed on stop.
Default
.Ql <base>/ephemeral .
.It Va roots.mountpoint
Filesystem location of the base.
Default
.Ql /Capabilities .
.It Va ephemeral.sync
The
.Ql sync
property applied to ephemeral datasets.
Default
.Ql disabled
for throughput.
.It Va default_refquota
Default per-claim space ceiling, in bytes, applied as the dataset
.Sy refquota
so no single claim can fill the pool and starve other tenants.
UCL size suffixes such as
.Ql 1gb
are accepted and pre-multiplied.
A per-request quota override (see
.Xr bsdfilesystem_request_quota 3 )
supersedes this default; a value of 0 disables the ceiling.
Default
.Ql 1gb
.Pq 1 GiB .
.It Va reclaim_interval
Grace period, in seconds, between reclaim timer passes that destroy orphaned
ephemeral datasets.
Bounded to
.Ql 10 Ns .. Ns Ql 86400 ;
out-of-range, fractional, and nonfinite values are rejected.
Default
.Ql 300 .
.It Va staging_idle_grace
Legacy staging-age setting, accepted for configuration compatibility.
Automatic staging reclamation is suspended: age and mount state do not establish
transaction ownership or safe recursive deletion.
Startup and idle sweeps preserve unresolved transaction datasets.
This value currently does not authorize deletion.
Bounded to
.Ql 1 Ns .. Ns Ql 86400 ;
out-of-range, fractional, and nonfinite values are rejected.
Default
.Ql 300 .
.It Va open_paths
Array of per-label isolated-open policy entries for the
.Xr bsdfilesystem 8
OPEN operation, which lets a sandboxed service reach a device node, shared
directory, or config file it cannot open by path itself.
The policy is
.Em default-deny :
absent, no path is openable.
Each entry is an object with the keys:
.Bl -tag -width ".Va prefix" -offset indent
.It Va label
the exact client channel label the entry grants to
.Pq required .
.It Va path
one absolute path
.Pq required ;
no empty or
.Ql ..
traversal component.
.It Va rights
a required array drawn from
.Ql read ,
.Ql write ,
.Ql exec ,
.Ql lookup ,
and
.Ql ioctl ;
at least one is required.
.It Va prefix
optional boolean.
When true,
.Va path
matches the path itself or a single trailing component
.Pq a device unit, e.g. Pa /dev/vhid No matching Pa /dev/vhidN ,
never a deeper subdirectory.
When false or absent, only an exact path match is granted.
.It Va verify
Optional boolean, default false.
When true, open with
.Dv O_VERIFY
and require a regular file.
Only exact paths and read or execute rights are permitted.
The shipped authentication policy and account-file entries enable this option.
The broker also opens its own configuration with
.Dv O_VERIFY .
These checks depend on the system's veriexec enforcement state and enrolled
fingerprints; enabling this option alone does not establish a trusted boot
or prevent changes while veriexec is inactive.
.El
.El
.Sh FILES
.Bl -tag -width ".Pa /Capabilities/Config/bsdfilesystem.ucl" -compact
.It Pa /Capabilities/Config/bsdfilesystem.ucl
the file described here
.El
.Sh EXAMPLES
Back
.Pa /Capabilities
with a dedicated pool:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
pool = "tank";
ephemeral { sync = "standard"; }
.Ed
.Pp
Cap every claim at 1 GiB by default and grant one label read access to a
device unit family:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
default_refquota = 1gb;
open_paths = [
    { label = "system.Bluetooth"; path = "/dev/vhid"; prefix = true;
      rights = ["read", "write", "ioctl"]; }
]
.Ed
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr libbsdfilesystem 3 ,
.Xr trustedzfs 3 ,
.Xr tzfsctl 8 ,
.Xr bsdfilesystem 8
.Sh AUTHORS
.An Kory Heard
